.TH DISPARPDF "1" "October 2026" "disparPDF 1.0.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
disparPDF, disparPDFc \- compare two PDF files textually or visually
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B disparPDF
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,FILE1 \/\fR[\fI\,FILE2\/\fR]]
.br
.B disparPDF
\fI\,--batch \/\fR[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,FILE1 FILE2\/\fR
.br
.B disparPDFc
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,FILE1 FILE2\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare two PDF files and show their differences.
.PP
The files are optional and are normally chosen in the window.  With \fB\-\-batch\fR,
they are compared without a window, and the result code (see below) is
printed.
.PP
By default the comparison is of the words on each pair of pages, but
comparing character by character is also supported (e.g., for
logographic languages).  And there's also support for comparing the
pages by appearance (for example, if a diagram is changed or if a
paragraph is reformatted, or a font changed).  It is also possible to
compare particular pages or page ranges, and to pair each page of one
file with a page further on in the other, for when pages have been
inserted or removed.
.PP
The differences can be saved as a PDF file, with the pages side by side
and the differences highlighted.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-batch ,
the files are compared without a window, which needs no display, and the
result code is printed; by default the appearance of the pages is
compared.  Settings such as the zoom, the tolerances and the margins to
leave out can be given in a file
.RB ( \-\-settings ),
in the same format as the configuration file (see
.BR FILES ).
.PP
.B disparPDFc
is a link to
.BR disparPDF ,
which, run by that name, is in batch mode without
.BR \-\-batch ,
and shows the window only when given
.BR \-\-interactive .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-appearance\fR
compare the appearance of the pages (the default in
batch mode)
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-characters\fR
compare the text character by character
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-words\fR
compare the text word by word (the default otherwise)
.TP
\fB\-\-any\-extension\fR
accept files whose names do not end in .pdf
.TP
\fB\-\-language\fR=\fI\,LANG\/\fR
use the given translation language, e.g., en for
English, cz for Czech; English is used if there is
no translation
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR=\fI\,2\/\fR
write the text fed to the sequence matcher into
temporary files (e.g., \fI\,/tmp/page1.txt\/\fP)
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR=\fI\,3\/\fR
as \fB\-\-debug\fR=\fI\,2\/\fR, but also with the coordinates, in y, x
order
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
display this help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
output version information and exit
.SS "Batch mode options:"
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-batch\fR
compare without a window
.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
show the window (the default, except as disparPDFc)
.TP
\fB\-\-outType\fR=\fI\,0\/\fR
print only the result code (the default)
.TP
\fB\-\-outType\fR=\fI\,1\/\fR
print the result code and a description
.TP
\fB\-\-pages\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
compare N pages (default all)
.TP
\fB\-\-startPage1\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
start at page N of FILE1
.TP
\fB\-\-startPage2\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
start at page N of FILE2
.TP
\fB\-\-pdfdiff\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
save the pages that differ, highlighted, to FILE
.TP
\fB\-\-xmlResult\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
write the result, in XML, to FILE
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR=\fI\,KEY\/\fR
record KEY in the XML result
.TP
\fB\-\-settings\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
read settings (zoom, margins, tolerances, colors,
etc.) from FILE, in INI format, instead of using
the defaults
.TP
\fB\-\-compareFonts\fR
also compare the fonts the files use
.SS "Result codes, printed in batch mode and also the exit status (modulo 256):"
.TP
0
the files are the same
.TP
1
the files differ
.TP
2
the files have different numbers of pages
.TP
3
a start page is beyond the end of its file
.TP
4
a file has fewer pages than \fB\-\-pages\fR asks for
.TP
5
the same file was given twice
.TP
6
the files use different fonts (with \fB\-\-compareFonts\fR)
.TP
\fB\-1\fR
a command line error
.TP
\fB\-3\fR, \fB\-4\fR
FILE1 or FILE2 cannot be read
.TP
\fB\-5\fR
a page cannot be read
.TP
\fB\-6\fR, \fB\-7\fR
the \fB\-\-pdfdiff\fR or \fB\-\-xmlResult\fR file cannot be written
.PP
